This MIT license covers all original DigiChat code, scripts, build and CI
configuration, documentation, and other authored repository material except
the third-party and franchise material identified below.

Digimon and all related names, characters, and media are trademarks of Bandai.
This is an unofficial, non-commercial fan project, not affiliated with,
sponsored by, or endorsed by Bandai or Toei Animation, and it claims no
ownership of their material. No Digimon artwork is included in this repository.

`data/lineages.json` is MIT as to its curation, structure, and ordering. The
species names inside it are Bandai trademarks, used nominatively to identify the
characters; that use is not licensed here and is not the author's to grant.

`data/digimon-names.json` is a curated reference assembled from name fields
returned by the digi-api.com API and Shadow Smith's Digimon API. digi-api.com
credits official and fan sources, mainly Wikimon.net. Wikimon contributor
content is available under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 (CC
BY-SA 3.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/ . To the extent
that the reference file adapts that content, it remains under CC BY-SA 3.0
rather than the MIT license above.

DigiChat extracted only name fields, combined the two API result sets,
normalized and curated the entries, and added a documented set of manually
verified English aliases. This notice credits the APIs as sources; it does not
claim that either API operator grants a blanket CC license over all API
content. See the README section "License and IP" and the metadata at the top of
`data/digimon-names.json` for source links and modification details.
